IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa27-definitions`

-- coa27-transfer.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 42 Chapter 6 (part): ss 1253A to 1253F, "Cooperation with foreign
-- competent authorities", "Transfer of papers to third countries" and the publication of working arrangements,
-- lines 17757-17866 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1 (the law, objectively); part agent coa27.
--
-- READING A RESULT (the rule of 2026-10-29): JUST TRUE the text says yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words ("if",
-- "unless", "must not", "Nothing ... authorises", "need not"); NOTHING the text does not decide (silent, limited by its own wording,
-- points outside the text). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE. "must not ... unless X": X not met is JUST FALSE; X met is
-- NOTHING where the text only makes X a necessary condition (the ruling of 2026-11-05 leaves "unless" once met to the encoder; fork F-D).
-- DATES. "Within 28 days following the date on which he receives the request" excludes the day of receipt: the last day is the
-- date of receipt plus 28 (fork F-B: the other reading counts the day of receipt as day one).
-- Every name begins with the section label it implements.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1253A Requests to foreign competent authorities
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17759 | The Secretary of State may request from ... a third country competent authority such assistance, information or investigation as he may reasonably require in connection with the exercise of his functions under this Part.
@ref s 1253A Requests to foreign competent authorities (src:17759-17759)
GIVEN `the request is made to a third country competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance, information or investigation is such as he may reasonably require in connection with the exercise of his functions under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253A the Secretary of State may request assistance, information or investigation` MEANS
    IF `the request is made to a third country competent authority` AND `the assistance, information or investigation is such as he may reasonably require in connection with the exercise of his functions under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may request from ... a third country competent authority such assistance, information or investigation as he may reasonably require"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1253B Requests from approved third country competent authorities
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17769 | (3) But the Secretary of State need not take steps to comply with a request under subsection (1) if—
-- src:17770 | (a) he considers that complying with the request may prejudice the sovereignty, security or public order of the United Kingdom;
-- src:17771 | (b) legal proceedings have been brought in the United Kingdom (whether continuing or not) in relation to the persons and matters to which the request relates; or
-- src:17772 | (c) disciplinary action has been taken by a recognised supervisory body in relation to the persons and matters to which the request relates.
@ref s 1253B(3) Requests from approved third country competent authorities: when he need not comply (src:17769-17772)
GIVEN `he considers that complying with the request may prejudice the sovereignty, security or public order of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `legal proceedings have been brought in the United Kingdom (whether continuing or not) in relation to the persons and matters to which the request relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `disciplinary action has been taken by a recognised supervisory body in relation to the persons and matters to which the request relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253B(3) the Secretary of State need not take steps to comply with the request` MEANS
    IF       `he considers that complying with the request may prejudice the sovereignty, security or public order of the United Kingdom`
          OR `legal proceedings have been brought in the United Kingdom (whether continuing or not) in relation to the persons and matters to which the request relates`
          OR `disciplinary action has been taken by a recognised supervisory body in relation to the persons and matters to which the request relates`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "need not take steps to comply with a request under subsection (1) if" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: fork F-D)

-- src:17761 | (1) The Secretary of State must take all necessary steps to—
-- src:17762 | (a) ensure that an investigation is carried out, or
-- src:17763 | (b) provide any other assistance or information,
-- src:17764 | if requested to do so by an approved third country competent authority ....
@ref s 1253B(1) Requests from approved third country competent authorities: the duty (src:17761-17764)
GIVEN `an approved third country competent authority has requested an investigation, or other assistance or information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a case within subsection (3) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253B(1) the Secretary of State must take all necessary steps to comply with the request` MEANS
    IF NOT `an approved third country competent authority has requested an investigation, or other assistance or information`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if requested to do so by an approved third country competent authority"
    ELSE IF `a case within subsection (3) applies`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (3), "need not take steps to comply with a request under subsection (1) if"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:17765 | (1A) Where the request includes a request for the transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports, the Secretary of State must act in accordance with section 1253D.
@ref s 1253B(1A) Requests from approved third country competent authorities: transfer of papers (src:17765-17765)
GIVEN `the request includes a request for the transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253B(1A) the Secretary of State must act in accordance with section 1253D` MEANS
    IF `the request includes a request for the transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the request includes a request for the transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports"

-- src:17766 | (2) Within 28 days following the date on which he receives the request, the Secretary of State must—
-- src:17767 | (a) provide the assistance or information required by the requesting authority under subsection (1)(b), or
-- src:17768 | (b) notify the requesting authority of the reasons why he has not done so.
@ref s 1253B(2) Requests from approved third country competent authorities: the 28 days (src:17766-17768)
GIVEN `the date on which he receives the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1253B(2) the last day of the period of 28 days following the date of receipt` MEANS
    `the date on which he receives the request` PLUS 28 -- "following the date": the day of receipt is not counted (fork F-B)

@ref s 1253B(2) Requests from approved third country competent authorities: whether he complied in time (src:17766-17768)
GIVEN `the date on which he receives the request` IS A DATE
      `the date he provided the assistance or information, or notified the reasons why he has not (NOTHING if he has done neither)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253B(2) the Secretary of State has complied with subsection (2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date he provided the assistance or information, or notified the reasons why he has not (NOTHING if he has done neither)`
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        IF d AT MOST `s 1253B(2) the last day of the period of 28 days following the date of receipt` `the date on which he receives the request`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 28 days following the date on which he receives the request, the Secretary of State must" (a period fixed in the text's own words: the ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the date as at which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `s 1253B(2) the last day of the period of 28 days following the date of receipt` `the date on which he receives the request`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the 28 days have run out with neither act done
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 28 days are still running, so the duty has not yet been met or missed

-- THE UNIT IS DAYS, AND ONLY THIS COMMENT SAYS SO. #TRACE time 0 is the date of receipt; "within 28 days following" that date ends at
-- time 28. The stable binary cannot #ASSERT on a deontic value, so the twin function above carries the counted assertions.
DECLARE `s 1253B act` IS ONE OF
    `s 1253B provide the assistance or information required, or notify the reasons why not`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 1253B act`
`s 1253B(2) the Secretary of State must provide the assistance or notify the reasons` MEANS
    PARTY `Secretary of State`
    MUST `s 1253B provide the assistance or information required, or notify the reasons why not`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `Secretary of State` BECAUSE "the Secretary of State neither provided the assistance or information nor notified the reasons within 28 days following the date on which he received the request"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1253C Notification to approved third country competent authorities
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17775 | (1) If the Secretary of State receives notice from a recognised supervisory body under section 1223A(1) (notification of matters relevant to approved third country competent authorities) that—
-- src:17776 | (a) a person has become eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor, or
-- src:17777 | (b) a person’s eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor has been withdrawn,
-- src:17778 | the Secretary of State must notify the relevant approved third country competent authority.
@ref s 1253C(1) Notification to approved third country competent authorities: notice from a recognised supervisory body (src:17775-17778)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has received notice from a recognised supervisory body under section 1223A(1) that a person has become eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor, or that a person's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253C(1) the Secretary of State must notify the relevant approved third country competent authority` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State has received notice from a recognised supervisory body under section 1223A(1) that a person has become eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor, or that a person's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor has been withdrawn`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Secretary of State receives notice ... the Secretary of State must notify" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: fork F-D)

-- src:17779 | (2) In subsection (1) “the relevant approved third country competent authority” means the approved third country competent authority which has approved the person concerned ... to carry out audits of annual accounts or consolidated accounts ....
@ref s 1253C(2) Notification: the relevant authority under subsection (1) (src:17779-17779)
GIVEN `the authority is an approved third country competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority has approved the person concerned to carry out audits of annual accounts or consolidated accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253C(2) the authority is the relevant approved third country competent authority` MEANS
    IF `the authority is an approved third country competent authority` AND `the authority has approved the person concerned to carry out audits of annual accounts or consolidated accounts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the relevant approved third country competent authority” means the approved third country competent authority which has approved the person concerned"

-- src:17780 | (3) The notification under subsection (1) must include the name of the person concerned and , in a case where a person’s eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor has been withdrawn, the reasons for the withdrawal.
@ref s 1253C(3) Notification: what it must include (src:17780-17780)
GIVEN `the notification is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253C(3) the notification must include the name of the person concerned` MEANS
    IF `the notification is made under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The notification under subsection (1)"

@ref s 1253C(3) Notification: reasons for a withdrawal (src:17780-17780)
GIVEN `the notification is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253C(3) the notification must include the reasons for the withdrawal` MEANS
    IF `the notification is made under subsection (1)` AND `the person's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor has been withdrawn`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a case where a person's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor has been withdrawn, the reasons for the withdrawal"

-- src:17781 | (4) The Secretary of State must notify the relevant approved third country competent authority if he has reasonable grounds for suspecting that—
-- src:17782 | (a) a person has contravened the law of the United Kingdom, or any equivalent third country or transitional third country, relating to audit, and
-- src:17783 | (b) the act or omission constituting that contravention took place on the territory of an equivalent third country or transitional third country.
@ref s 1253C(4) Notification: suspected contravention (src:17781-17783)
GIVEN `he has reasonable grounds for suspecting that a person has contravened the law of the United Kingdom, or any equivalent third country or transitional third country, relating to audit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he has reasonable grounds for suspecting that the act or omission constituting that contravention took place on the territory of an equivalent third country or transitional third country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253C(4) the Secretary of State must notify the relevant approved third country competent authority of the suspicion` MEANS
    IF       `he has reasonable grounds for suspecting that a person has contravened the law of the United Kingdom, or any equivalent third country or transitional third country, relating to audit`
         AND `he has reasonable grounds for suspecting that the act or omission constituting that contravention took place on the territory of an equivalent third country or transitional third country`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State must notify the relevant approved third country competent authority if he has reasonable grounds for suspecting that" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: fork F-D)

-- src:17784 | (5) In subsection (4) “the relevant approved third country competent authority” means the approved third country competent authority for the country or territory in which the suspected contravention took place.
@ref s 1253C(5) Notification: the relevant authority under subsection (4) (src:17784-17784)
GIVEN `the authority is the approved third country competent authority for the country or territory in which the suspected contravention took place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253C(5) the authority is the relevant approved third country competent authority for the suspicion` MEANS
    IF `the authority is the approved third country competent authority for the country or territory in which the suspected contravention took place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the relevant approved third country competent authority” means the approved third country competent authority for the country or territory in which the suspected contravention took place"

-- src:17785 | (6) The notification under subsection (4) must include the name of the person concerned and the grounds for the Secretary of State's suspicion.
@ref s 1253C(6) Notification: what it must include (src:17785-17785)
GIVEN `the notification is made under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253C(6) the notification must include the name of the person concerned and the grounds for the suspicion` MEANS
    IF `the notification is made under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The notification under subsection (4)"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1253D to 1253DE Transfer of audit working papers to third countries
-- =========================================================================================================

-- The three routes of s 1253D(1).
DECLARE `s 1253D(1) route` IS ONE OF
    `s 1253D(1)(a) transfer by the Secretary of State (section 1253DA)`
    `s 1253D(1)(b) transfer by a statutory auditor with the approval of the Secretary of State (section 1253DB)`
    `s 1253D(1)(c) transfer by a statutory auditor for the purposes of investigation of an auditor (section 1253DC)`
    `s 1253D(1) some other route`

-- src:17788 | (1) Audit working papers and investigation reports must not be transferred to a third country competent authority unless the third country competent authority is an approved third country competent authority and the transfers are made in accordance with—
-- src:17789 | (a) section 1253DA (transfer by Secretary of State),
-- src:17790 | (b) section 1253DB (transfer by statutory auditor with approval of Secretary of State), or
-- src:17791 | (c) section 1253DC (transfer by statutory auditor for purposes of investigation of auditor).
@ref s 1253D(1) Restriction on transfer of audit working papers: the restriction (src:17788-17791)
GIVEN `the authority is an approved third country competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      route IS A `s 1253D(1) route`
      `the transfer is made in accordance with the section the route names` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253D(1) the transfer to the third country competent authority is permitted` MEANS
    IF NOT `the authority is an approved third country competent authority`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be transferred to a third country competent authority unless the third country competent authority is an approved third country competent authority"
    ELSE CONSIDER route
         WHEN `s 1253D(1) some other route` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless ... the transfers are made in accordance with— (a) section 1253DA, (b) section 1253DB, or (c) section 1253DC"
         OTHERWISE `the transfer is made in accordance with the section the route names`
         -- the route's own section decides: JUST TRUE where it says so, JUST FALSE where its conditions fail, NOTHING where it points outside the text

-- src:17793 | (3) Nothing in the sections referred to in subsection (1) authorises the making of a disclosure in contravention of the data protection legislation.
@ref s 1253D(3) Restriction on transfer of audit working papers: data protection (src:17793-17793)
GIVEN `the disclosure would be made in contravention of the data protection legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253D(3) the sections referred to in subsection (1) authorise the disclosure` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure would be made in contravention of the data protection legislation`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in the sections referred to in subsection (1) authorises the making of a disclosure in contravention of the data protection legislation"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection only withholds authority

-- s 1253DD says when a transfer must not take place without the express agreement of another authority. The answers come first
-- because ss 1253DA and 1253DB read them.
-- src:17816 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:17817 | (a) an approved third country competent authority makes a request to the Secretary of State for the transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports which relate to the audit of the consolidated accounts of a group, and
-- src:17818 | (b) the audit working papers and investigation reports that are the subject of the request—
-- src:17819 | (i) have been created by the auditor of a subsidiary that is located in an equivalent third country or transitional third country in relation to the audit of that subsidiary, and
-- src:17820 | (ii) are in the possession of a statutory auditor.
@ref s 1253DD(1) Agreement of third country competent authority: when the section applies (src:17816-17820)
GIVEN `an approved third country competent authority has made a request to the Secretary of State for the transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports which relate to the audit of the consolidated accounts of a group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the papers have been created by the auditor of a subsidiary located in an equivalent third country or transitional third country in relation to the audit of that subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the papers are in the possession of a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253DD(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF       `an approved third country competent authority has made a request to the Secretary of State for the transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports which relate to the audit of the consolidated accounts of a group`
         AND `the papers have been created by the auditor of a subsidiary located in an equivalent third country or transitional third country in relation to the audit of that subsidiary`
         AND `the papers are in the possession of a statutory auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where"

-- src:17821 | (2) In the case of a transfer by the Secretary of State under section 1253DA, the transfer must not take place unless the third country competent authority responsible for the auditor of the subsidiary has given its express agreement to the transfer.
@ref s 1253DD(2) Agreement of third country competent authority: transfer by the Secretary of State (src:17821-17821)
GIVEN `this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third country competent authority responsible for the auditor of the subsidiary has given its express agreement to the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253DD(2) the transfer by the Secretary of State under section 1253DA must not take place` MEANS
    IF `this section applies` AND (NOT `the third country competent authority responsible for the auditor of the subsidiary has given its express agreement to the transfer`)
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the text says the transfer "must not take place unless" the express agreement has been given
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the transfer must not take place unless ... express agreement"; this subsection does not say a transfer with agreement may take place

-- src:17822 | (3) In the case of a transfer by a statutory auditor under section 1253DB, the Secretary of State must not approve the transfer unless the third country competent authority responsible for the auditor of the subsidiary has given its express agreement to the transfer.
@ref s 1253DD(3) Agreement of third country competent authority: approval of a transfer by a statutory auditor (src:17822-17822)
GIVEN `this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third country competent authority responsible for the auditor of the subsidiary has given its express agreement to the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253DD(3) the Secretary of State must not approve the transfer under section 1253DB` MEANS
    IF `this section applies` AND (NOT `the third country competent authority responsible for the auditor of the subsidiary has given its express agreement to the transfer`)
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the text says the Secretary of State "must not approve the transfer unless" the express agreement has been given
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must not approve the transfer unless ... express agreement"

-- src:17795 | (1) The Secretary of State may transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to an approved third country competent authority if the following conditions are met (but see also section 1253DD).
-- src:17796 | (2) The first condition is that the authority has made a request to the Secretary of State for the transfer of the audit working papers and investigation reports.
-- src:17797 | (3) The second condition is that the audit working papers and investigation reports relate to audits of companies that—
-- src:17798 | (a) have issued securities in the third country in which the authority is established, or
-- src:17799 | (b) form part of a group issuing statutory consolidated accounts in that third country.
-- src:17800 | (4) The third condition is that the authority has entered into arrangements with the Secretary of State in accordance with section 1253E.
@ref s 1253DA Transfer by Secretary of State (src:17795-17800)
GIVEN `the authority has made a request to the Secretary of State for the transfer of the audit working papers and investigation reports` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the papers relate to audits of companies that have issued securities in the third country in which the authority is established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the papers relate to audits of companies that form part of a group issuing statutory consolidated accounts in that third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority has entered into arrangements with the Secretary of State in accordance with section 1253E` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 1253DD(2) says the transfer must not take place` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253DA(1) the Secretary of State may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` MEANS
    IF       `the authority has made a request to the Secretary of State for the transfer of the audit working papers and investigation reports`
         AND (`the papers relate to audits of companies that have issued securities in the third country in which the authority is established`
              OR `the papers relate to audits of companies that form part of a group issuing statutory consolidated accounts in that third country`)
         AND `the authority has entered into arrangements with the Secretary of State in accordance with section 1253E`
    THEN IF `section 1253DD(2) says the transfer must not take place` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 1253DD(2), "the transfer must not take place unless"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may transfer ... if the following conditions are met" (name test of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q5)

-- src:17802 | (1) A statutory auditor may transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to an approved third country competent authority if the transfer is made—
-- src:17803 | (a) with the prior approval of the Secretary of State, and
-- src:17804 | (b) in accordance with rules of a recognised supervisory body meeting the requirements of paragraph 16AA of Schedule 10.
-- src:17805 | (2) The Secretary of State must not approve a transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports to an approved third country competent authority for the purposes of this section unless the following conditions are met (see also section 1253DD).
-- src:17806 | (3) The first condition is that the authority has made a request to the Secretary of State for the transfer of the audit working papers and investigation reports.
-- src:17807 | (4) The second condition is that the audit working papers and investigation reports relate to audits of companies that—
-- src:17808 | (a) have issued securities in the third country in which the authority is established, or
-- src:17809 | (b) form part of a group issuing statutory consolidated accounts in that third country.
-- src:17810 | (5) The third condition is that the authority has entered into arrangements with the Secretary of State in accordance with section 1253E.
@ref s 1253DB Transfer by statutory auditor with approval of Secretary of State (src:17802-17810)
GIVEN `the transfer is made with the prior approval of the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is made in accordance with rules of a recognised supervisory body meeting the requirements of paragraph 16AA of Schedule 10` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253DB(1) the statutory auditor may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` MEANS
    IF `the transfer is made with the prior approval of the Secretary of State` AND `the transfer is made in accordance with rules of a recognised supervisory body meeting the requirements of paragraph 16AA of Schedule 10`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may transfer ... if the transfer is made— (a) with the prior approval ... and (b) in accordance with rules" (name test of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q6)

@ref s 1253DB Transfer by statutory auditor with approval of Secretary of State: the approval (src:17805-17810)
GIVEN `the authority has made a request to the Secretary of State for the transfer of the audit working papers and investigation reports` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the papers relate to audits of companies that have issued securities in the third country in which the authority is established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the papers relate to audits of companies that form part of a group issuing statutory consolidated accounts in that third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority has entered into arrangements with the Secretary of State in accordance with section 1253E` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 1253DD(3) says the Secretary of State must not approve the transfer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253DB(2) the Secretary of State may approve the transfer` MEANS
    IF       NOT (`the authority has made a request to the Secretary of State for the transfer of the audit working papers and investigation reports`
                  AND (`the papers relate to audits of companies that have issued securities in the third country in which the authority is established`
                       OR `the papers relate to audits of companies that form part of a group issuing statutory consolidated accounts in that third country`)
                  AND `the authority has entered into arrangements with the Secretary of State in accordance with section 1253E`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not approve a transfer ... unless the following conditions are met"
    ELSE IF `section 1253DD(3) says the Secretary of State must not approve the transfer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 1253DD(3), "must not approve the transfer unless"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the conditions are necessary, and the text does not say they are enough to approve

-- src:17812 | A statutory auditor may transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority if the transfer is made—
-- src:17813 | (a) for the purposes of an investigation of an auditor or audit firm, and
-- src:17814 | (b) in accordance with rules of a recognised supervisory body meeting the requirements of paragraph 16AB of Schedule 10.
@ref s 1253DC Transfer by statutory auditor for purposes of investigation of auditor (src:17812-17814)
GIVEN `the transfer is made for the purposes of an investigation of an auditor or audit firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is made in accordance with rules of a recognised supervisory body meeting the requirements of paragraph 16AB of Schedule 10` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253DC the statutory auditor may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the third country competent authority` MEANS
    IF `the transfer is made for the purposes of an investigation of an auditor or audit firm` AND `the transfer is made in accordance with rules of a recognised supervisory body meeting the requirements of paragraph 16AB of Schedule 10`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may transfer ... if the transfer is made— (a) for the purposes of an investigation ... and (b) in accordance with rules" (name test of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q7)

-- src:17824 | (1) This section applies in the case of a transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports if—
-- src:17825 | (a) it is a transfer to an approved third country competent authority ...,
-- src:17826 | (b) it is a transfer under section 1253DA or 1253DB, and
-- src:17827 | (c) it is to take place by means of an inspection in the United Kingdom by the authority.
@ref s 1253DE(1) Transfer by means of inspection: when the section applies (src:17824-17827)
GIVEN `the transfer is to an approved third country competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is under section 1253DA or 1253DB` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is to take place by means of an inspection in the United Kingdom by the authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253DE(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the transfer is to an approved third country competent authority` AND `the transfer is under section 1253DA or 1253DB` AND `the transfer is to take place by means of an inspection in the United Kingdom by the authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies in the case of a transfer ... if"

-- src:17828 | (2) The Secretary of State must participate in the inspection.
@ref s 1253DE(2) Transfer by means of inspection: participation (src:17828-17828)
GIVEN `this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253DE(2) the Secretary of State must participate in the inspection` MEANS
    IF `this section applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (1), "This section applies ... if" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: fork F-D)

-- src:17829 | (3) The inspection must be under the leadership of the Secretary of State unless the Secretary of State otherwise permits.
@ref s 1253DE(3) Transfer by means of inspection: leadership (src:17829-17829)
GIVEN `this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State otherwise permits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253DE(3) the inspection must be under the leadership of the Secretary of State` MEANS
    IF NOT `this section applies`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (1), "This section applies ... if"
    ELSE IF `the Secretary of State otherwise permits`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Secretary of State otherwise permits"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1253E Working arrangements for transfer of papers
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17831 | (1) The Secretary of State may enter into arrangements with a third country competent authority relating to the transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports—
-- src:17832 | (a) from the third country competent authority or a third country auditor regulated by that authority to the Secretary of State, and
-- src:17833 | (b) from the Secretary of State or a statutory auditor to the third country competent authority.
@ref s 1253E(1) Working arrangements: the power (src:17831-17833)
GIVEN `the arrangements are with a third country competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangements relate to the transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports from the authority or a third country auditor it regulates to the Secretary of State, or from the Secretary of State or a statutory auditor to the authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253E(1) the Secretary of State may enter into the arrangements` MEANS
    IF `the arrangements are with a third country competent authority` AND `the arrangements relate to the transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports from the authority or a third country auditor it regulates to the Secretary of State, or from the Secretary of State or a statutory auditor to the authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may enter into arrangements with a third country competent authority relating to the transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports"

-- What the arrangements must provide (subsections (2), (3), (5), (6), (7A)): the terms a set of arrangements contains.
DECLARE `s 1253E arrangements` HAS
    `s 1253E(2) a request for a transfer is accompanied by a statement explaining the reasons for the request` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1253E(3)(a) the Secretary of State may not use the papers obtained except in connection with the functions in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1253E(3)(b) comparable provision for papers obtained by the third country competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1253E(5)(a) confidentiality obligations on the Secretary of State, those exercising his functions and those employed or formerly employed in discharging them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1253E(5)(b) comparable obligations on the third country competent authority and those involved in exercising its functions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1253E(5)(c) the commercial interests of any audited person are not undermined` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1253E(6)(a) the Secretary of State may refuse, or direct a statutory auditor to refuse, a request in a case mentioned in subsection (7)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1253E(6)(b) the third country competent authority has comparable rights` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1253E(7A)(a) the Secretary of State may only disclose confidential information received on the grounds stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1253E(7A)(b) the third country competent authority may only disclose confidential information received on the grounds stated` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:17834 | (2) The arrangements must provide that a request by the Secretary of State or the third country competent authority for a transfer mentioned in subsection (1) must be accompanied by a statement explaining the reasons for the request.
-- src:17835 | (3) The arrangements must—
-- src:17836 | (a) provide that the Secretary of State may not use audit working papers and investigation reports obtained from the third country competent authority or a third country auditor regulated by that authority except in connection with one or more of the functions mentioned in subsection (4), and
-- src:17837 | (b) include comparable provision in relation to audit working papers and investigation reports obtained by the third country competent authority from the Secretary of State or a statutory auditor.
-- src:17838 | (4) Those functions are—
-- src:17839 | (a) quality assurance functions which meet requirements equivalent to those of regulation 9 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016;
-- src:17840 | (b) investigation or disciplinary functions which meet requirements equivalent to those of regulations 5 to 8 and 10 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016;
-- src:17841 | (c) public oversight functions which meet requirements equivalent to those of regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016.
-- src:17842 | (5) The arrangements must—
-- src:17843 | (a) provide that the Secretary of State, a person exercising the functions of the Secretary of State and persons employed or formerly employed in discharging those functions must be subject to obligations of confidentiality as to personal data, professional secrets and sensitive commercial information contained in audit working papers and investigation reports transferred to the Secretary of State, ...
-- src:17844 | (b) provide that the third country competent authority and persons involved in exercising its functions are subject to comparable obligations in relation to audit working papers and investigation reports transferred to the authority and
-- src:17845 | (c) ensure that the protection of the commercial interests of any audited person, including its industrial and intellectual property, is not undermined.
-- src:17846 | (6) The arrangements must—
-- src:17847 | (a) provide that the Secretary of State may refuse, or direct a statutory auditor to refuse, a request from the third country competent authority for a transfer of audit working papers and investigation reports in a case mentioned in subsection (7)(a) or (b), and
-- src:17848 | (b) provide that the third country competent authority has comparable rights in relation to a request from the Secretary of State.
-- src:17849 | (7) Those cases are—
-- src:17850 | (a) where the transfer of the papers would adversely affect the sovereignty, security or public order ...of the United Kingdom;
-- src:17851 | (b) where legal proceedings have been brought in the United Kingdom (whether continuing or not) in relation to the persons and matters to which the request relates.
-- src:17852 | (7A) The arrangements must—
-- src:17853 | (a) provide that the Secretary of State may only disclose confidential information received from the third country competent authority—
-- src:17854 | (i) with the agreement of that authority or for purposes for which that authority has given its agreement,
-- src:17855 | (ii) where disclosure is required by law, or
-- src:17856 | (iii) where disclosure is necessary in connection with legal proceedings, and
-- src:17857 | (b) provide that the third country competent authority may only disclose confidential information received from the Secretary of State—
-- src:17858 | (i) with the Secretary of State’s agreement or for purposes for which the Secretary of State has given agreement,
-- src:17859 | (ii) where disclosure is required by law, or
-- src:17860 | (iii) where disclosure is necessary in connection with legal proceedings.
@ref s 1253E(2)-(7A) Working arrangements: what the arrangements must provide (src:17834-17860)
GIVEN a IS A `s 1253E arrangements`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253E(2)-(7A) the arrangements contain the terms the section requires` MEANS
    IF       a's `s 1253E(2) a request for a transfer is accompanied by a statement explaining the reasons for the request`
         AND a's `s 1253E(3)(a) the Secretary of State may not use the papers obtained except in connection with the functions in subsection (4)`
         AND a's `s 1253E(3)(b) comparable provision for papers obtained by the third country competent authority`
         AND a's `s 1253E(5)(a) confidentiality obligations on the Secretary of State, those exercising his functions and those employed or formerly employed in discharging them`
         AND a's `s 1253E(5)(b) comparable obligations on the third country competent authority and those involved in exercising its functions`
         AND a's `s 1253E(5)(c) the commercial interests of any audited person are not undermined`
         AND a's `s 1253E(6)(a) the Secretary of State may refuse, or direct a statutory auditor to refuse, a request in a case mentioned in subsection (7)(a) or (b)`
         AND a's `s 1253E(6)(b) the third country competent authority has comparable rights`
         AND a's `s 1253E(7A)(a) the Secretary of State may only disclose confidential information received on the grounds stated`
         AND a's `s 1253E(7A)(b) the third country competent authority may only disclose confidential information received on the grounds stated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The arrangements must provide ... must ... must" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-D)

-- (4): the functions to which the papers may be put. Each is a function "which meets requirements equivalent to" a regulation of the
-- Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016, which is outside the sources: the equivalence is an input.
DECLARE `s 1253E(4) function` IS ONE OF
    `s 1253E(4)(a) quality assurance functions (equivalent to regulation 9)`
    `s 1253E(4)(b) investigation or disciplinary functions (equivalent to regulations 5 to 8 and 10)`
    `s 1253E(4)(c) public oversight functions (equivalent to regulation 3)`
    `s 1253E(4) some other function`

-- src:17838 | (4) Those functions are—
-- src:17839 | (a) quality assurance functions which meet requirements equivalent to those of regulation 9 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016;
-- src:17840 | (b) investigation or disciplinary functions which meet requirements equivalent to those of regulations 5 to 8 and 10 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016;
-- src:17841 | (c) public oversight functions which meet requirements equivalent to those of regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016.
@ref s 1253E(4) Working arrangements: the functions (src:17838-17841)
GIVEN f IS A `s 1253E(4) function`
      `the function meets requirements equivalent to those of the regulation or regulations named` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253E(4) the function is one of those functions` MEANS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `s 1253E(4) some other function` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Those functions are— (a) ... (b) ... (c)"
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the function meets requirements equivalent to those of the regulation or regulations named`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "functions which meet requirements equivalent to those of regulation"

-- src:17849 | (7) Those cases are—
-- src:17850 | (a) where the transfer of the papers would adversely affect the sovereignty, security or public order ...of the United Kingdom;
-- src:17851 | (b) where legal proceedings have been brought in the United Kingdom (whether continuing or not) in relation to the persons and matters to which the request relates.
@ref s 1253E(7) Working arrangements: the cases (src:17849-17851)
GIVEN `the transfer of the papers would adversely affect the sovereignty, security or public order of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `legal proceedings have been brought in the United Kingdom (whether continuing or not) in relation to the persons and matters to which the request relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253E(7) the case is one mentioned` MEANS
    IF `the transfer of the papers would adversely affect the sovereignty, security or public order of the United Kingdom`
       OR `legal proceedings have been brought in the United Kingdom (whether continuing or not) in relation to the persons and matters to which the request relates`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Those cases are— (a) ... (b)"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1253F Publication of working arrangements
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17864 | If the Secretary of State enters into working arrangements in accordance with section 1253E, he must publish on a website without undue delay—
-- src:17865 | (a) the name of the third country competent authority with which he has entered into such arrangements, and
-- src:17866 | (b) the country or territory in which it is established.
@ref s 1253F Publication of working arrangements: the duty (src:17864-17866)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has entered into working arrangements in accordance with section 1253E` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253F the Secretary of State must publish on a website the name of the authority and the country or territory in which it is established` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State has entered into working arrangements in accordance with section 1253E`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Secretary of State enters into working arrangements in accordance with section 1253E, he must publish" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: fork F-D)

@ref s 1253F Publication of working arrangements: whether it has been met (src:17864-17866)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has entered into working arrangements in accordance with section 1253E` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he has published on a website the name of the third country competent authority and the country or territory in which it is established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he published without undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253F the Secretary of State has met the duty to publish` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Secretary of State has entered into working arrangements in accordance with section 1253E`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Secretary of State enters into working arrangements"
    ELSE IF `he has published on a website the name of the third country competent authority and the country or territory in which it is established` AND `he published without undue delay`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "he must publish on a website without undue delay" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-D; "undue delay" is a judgment taken as a plain input)
